  "scope_id": "HOLE-CRITERION-COLOURING-20261019-001",
  "title": "Braun's Res(⊕) bound extends to more pigeons and to bit-colouring",
  "subject": "Holes in partial-colouring shapes and Res(⊕) lower bounds for bit-encoded colouring",
  "conclusion": "For l >= 32, every DAG-like Res(⊕) refutation of bit PHP with 2^l holes and m pigeons, for 2^l < m with 8192 m l^2 (2l+5) <= 4^l, has more than exp(4^l/(8192 m l^2)) lines, checked in Lean against Braun's replayed development. A proper colouring with m classes turns every bit-colouring refutation into one of bit PHP with m pigeons of the same size, so the bound covers every graph whose chromatic number lies in that range.",
